# Akoro Study-Prep — Master Plan (v7)

Supersedes v6. Written after a full read of the codebase. Corrects the
workspace location, replaces the designed context registry with the actual
`manifest.mjs`, documents every MD file that exists, updates the "what's
built" inventory, and identifies the two remaining gaps: operation-level
context switching and the streaming chat UI (SSE + client).

**Legend:** ✅ built and read in code · 🟡 exists, needs change · 🆕 not yet
built · ❓ not verified.

---

## 1. The idea in one paragraph

A learner asks to prepare for a test. A **study agent** (LLM) decides what to
look at next, calls a tool, and reads what comes back. A **harness** (code)
decides whether each call is allowed, then performs it. A **deterministic
education engine** (code) scores, applies thresholds, writes state and
evidence. A **context manager** (platform module) selects the minimum set of
MD files for the current operation and assembles the LLM's system prompt. The
agent never touches state, money or scores directly. The learner watches the
whole process stream live as collapsible thinking blocks, collapsible tool
groups, and plain-text activity messages.

```
